;; The oracle's class-script steps (test/oracle/expected/classes) whose recorded result needs
;; arbace.core loaded, which the Go build has not before its evaluator (B1a step 5): bin/c2g-check
;; counts a failing step listed here as "need core", not as a failure, and names a listed step
;; that passes (the list is then stale). Read with the Clojure reader. doc/go/C2G-NOTES.md,
;; phase 2A, "The steps that need arbace.core".
;;
;; Kinds of reasons:
;;   print-method  the JVM recorded core's printer (RT.print calls pr-on once
;;                 *print-initialized* is true); without core RT.print's own printer runs
;;   ns-maps       core's printer with *print-namespace-maps* true (bound by arbace.main)
;;   data-readers  core's default-data-readers (#inst, #uuid) and its *default-data-reader-fn*
;;                 (root nil; RT's root before core is an empty map)
;;   core-var      a var arbace.core defines
